The README drifts from the code in two places.

README:142-143 names the cache directory ~/.cache/www-metaforge/ and %LOCALAPPDATA%/www-metaforge/, but the code creates ~/.cache/metaforge/ (lib/WWW/MetaForge/Cache.pm:35-39, namespace default metaforge, :94-95), the same as the POD of Cache.pm:24 says. A user looks for the cache under ~/.cache/www-metaforge/, does not find it, and --no-cache or the deletion goes into the void.

README:169 lists 5 maps, the code has 6 (lib/WWW/MetaForge/ArcRaiders.pm:59 adds riven-tides and stella-montis, Changes:13 has them already).

Decide: the README names the cache directory that the code uses and lists the two maps that are missing.

Commit 1813891 auf Branch k14-k16: README nennt jetzt ~/.cache/metaforge/ (bzw. $XDG_CACHE_HOME/metaforge/) und %LOCALAPPDATA%/metaforge/, Kartenliste um riven-tides und stella-montis ergaenzt; POD der maps-Methode in lib/WWW/MetaForge/ArcRaiders.pm ergaenzt; Suite gruen (21 Dateien, 186 Tests). Geaenderte Zeilen: README.md:141-143, README.md:169, lib/WWW/MetaForge/ArcRaiders.pm:76.

